# PLANNED (not run yet): Gemma 3 27B Instruct (Google). One A100/H100 80GB, or a 48 GB GPU at 4 bits.
# Before running, check on Hugging Face:
#   - a 4-bit file SGLang serves (e.g. an AWQ or GPTQ release, or Google's QAT int4 checkpoint);
#   - a published EAGLE-3 head for Gemma 3 27B; if none, the pipeline needs the "from scratch" path (not built yet);
#   - SpecForge chat template for Gemma (add "gemma" to regen.py HEADERS: '<start_of_turn>model\n');
#   - Gemma 3 is multimodal and uses sliding-window attention: confirm SGLang speculative decoding supports it.
MODEL=gemma3-27b
TARGET=CHECK-4BIT-REPO
PUB_HEAD=CHECK-EAGLE3-HEAD
OLLAMA_TAG=gemma3:27b
SF_TEMPLATE=gemma                            # verify the name in SpecForge
CHAT_KWARGS='{}'
SYSTEM_TURN=0
CTX=4096
